00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:21.090
We worked together.

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:23.370
Like on a team, me and Corky did.

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:33.440
Don't just stand there, come on.

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:00.530
Yes

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.350
I was looking for a girlfriend's apartment.

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:03.710
I don't think you'll find her here.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:05.130
There's only one apartment in this building.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.190
That's on the fourth floor.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:08.490
The rest of the building is full of dress manufacturers.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.890
Oh, thank you for telling me, but I think I'll just go in and check.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:14.310
I told you you wouldn't find her here.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.920
There's a guy in that apartment that kind of likes his privacy.

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.580
You'll get nothing but trouble if you go in there.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.870
But I'm sure I have the right address.

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.820
I have the number right here in my purse.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:28.400
Mr. You don't need to say anything else

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:29.830
I don't know what this is.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.310
I told you, you talked enough.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:34.300
I'm not afraid to use this gun, so you'd better do what I tell you to.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:37.890
What do you want me to do?

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:41.040
We're going to pay a little visit to your boss, Marty Stapka.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:42.450
Now get going.

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:53.580
Come faster, huh driver?

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.500
Any faster and we'll end up like O'Connor.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:57.250
Connor

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.340
Yeah, tell me about O'Connor, Marty kill him.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:00.340
No.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:01.610
What's the connection?

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.480
Ruth Calder?

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.380
You mean the girl that was killed in the accident?

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:08.680
She was running around with O'Connor when Marty wasn't looking.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.440
What's that got to do with O'Connor being murdered?

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.130
He wasn't murdered.

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:15.990
He was killed in the auto accident with Ruth.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:19.290
And now honey, the police found his body in the cellar.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.440
Where Marty put it.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.900
I found out that Ruth and O'Connor were going to someplace in Connecticut for dinner.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:29.780
So I have made Marty drive me out there to prove I was telling the truth.

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.580
And that's where the accident happened.

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:32.370
Yeah.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:35.900
They missed a curve in the road and ran into a stone wall.

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:37.710
Must have been going night-y.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:39.530
Both of them had been drinking.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:40.610
Thank you.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:43.270
Tell Mr.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.380
Tucker, you want to talk to me?

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:45.780
Get him to open the door.

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:50.360
And remember, I may not look very strong, but it doesn't take much strength to pull this trigger.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.680
Don't get any ideas about playing the big He-Man.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:06.210
Go ahead and knock.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.240
Yeah, who is it?

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:12.770
It's me, Marty.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:15.000
What are you doing up here, Reed?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.720
I told you to watch the downstairs door.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:18.900
I'm sorry, Marty, but I gotta see.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:19.420
It's important.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.070
Okay, just a minute.

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:28.180
Right, Mr. Stavker.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:29.330
Hands up.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.540
Sorry, boss, this dame surprised me.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.030
I didn't figure she was the type that had a gun on her purse.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.780
What is this? I don't know you.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:38.980
But I know you, Mr. Stapka.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.620
Now back up slowly. We're coming inside.

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:53.530
Closet.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:55.870
You're no closet.

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.620
What she wants, but you better do what she says.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:20:59.970
Go on, get in the closet.

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:18.170
Tell me what this is all about.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:20.400
I'll be glad to, Mr. Stuck.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.020
I've been looking forward to this conversation.

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:24.700
Sit down.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:36.790
knew that you were telling the truth about it no marty didn't know anything at first except that

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:43.410
she was dead kept saying her name over and over again like he could bring her back to life by

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:51.920
doing that then he got sore and blamed the whole thing on o'connor and he walked over to me and said

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:59.900
baby you gotta help me ruthie can't be found with this crumb thought i was carrying a torch

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:07.900
Yeah, he took O'Connor's body out of the car and drove it back to town, huh?

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:12.080
Yeah, this is it.

00:22:14.860 --> 00:22:16.510
Uh, wait here, honey.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:20.700
I'll say goodbyes to Marty if he's able to hear them.

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:26.880
I worshipped Ruth, Mr. Stupka, and you killed her.

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:29.980
Ruth was killed in an auto accident, you know that.

00:22:30.190 --> 00:22:34.040
You put her there. The police said she was speeding and drinking.

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:44.100
My sister never did things like that until she took up with you.

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:52.700
I'm going to shoot you.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:54.210
You got your facts wrong, lady.

00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:56.870
Your sister was as bad as they come.

00:22:57.770 --> 00:22:59.050
You stay out of this, Mr. Diamond.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:09.150
concern of yours. He's a cheap liar and a two-timer. Stop it. The very night she was killed, she was

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:13.310
double-crossing him for the kind of guy that you've never even heard of. He took the man's body out of

00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:18.120
the car. You're a liar. He risked his life so that your sister wouldn't be found dead in the company

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:25.900
of the cheapest trash there is. You know why I did it? Because he loved your sister every bit as much

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:29.920
as you did. No. No, you're not telling me.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:37.610
the truth. That I am, ma'am, and I can prove it. Now, you ask him if he loved your sister

00:23:37.610 --> 00:23:50.890
and you hold the gun in your hand. And if you don't believe it, who is it? Do you love

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:51.450
my sister?

00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:01.860
I still do.

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:17.670
Lieutenant

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:19.970
another thing diamond

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:23.540
If Marty Stopka hadn't said just the right words, that girl would have shot him.

00:24:23.710 --> 00:24:24.550
Yes, Lieutenant.

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:29.500
You all right, Lieutenant?

00:24:30.670 --> 00:24:31.910
You know where that would have left you?

00:24:32.230 --> 00:24:33.650
Practically an accomplice to murder.

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:36.390
Not to mention your earlier exploits.

00:24:36.590 --> 00:24:38.940
Assault and battery, breaking and entering,

00:24:39.990 --> 00:24:41.890
suppressing information, obstructing justice.

00:24:42.620 --> 00:24:43.820
And stop that gibbering.

00:24:46.580 --> 00:24:49.280
I'm still here, Lieutenant.

00:24:50.530 --> 00:24:53.020
Well, actually, you helped quite a few people,

00:24:53.060 --> 00:24:54.240
so I'm letting you off the hook.

00:24:56.050 --> 00:24:56.410
Night, Rick.

00:24:57.240 --> 00:24:58.000
Good night, Lieutenant.
